earth: your club has made it to the final for the first time in twenty years, and the whole club is going
scene: For the first time in twenty years the club has reached the final. The minibus is booked, the old banner is down from the loft, and on Saturday the whole club, players, families and old members, will be there.
scene W: {N} has turned up every week for years, in the rain, through the bad seasons. This is what all those wet evenings were for.
scene U: {N} has watched the other side play twice and has noticed things about them that nobody else at the club seems to have seen.
scene B: There will be a crowd, the local paper and the people who run the town. A big day is also a chance to be seen.
scene R: {N} has not slept properly all week. Saturday cannot come soon enough.
scene G: The old members still talk about the last final, twenty years ago, as if it were yesterday. Their photographs line the clubhouse wall.
